    {
      "id": "bool-3c7383",
      "name": "bool",
      "category": "AxisPositionGizmo",
      "signature": "bool(Target, Should Use Custom Destination Func)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "UAxisPositionGizmo*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Should Use Custom Destination Func",
          "type": ")>",
          "default": "[]("
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "TUniqueFunction<",
      "docs": "This gets checked to see if we should use the custom destination function to get a destination point for\nthe gizmo, rather than grabbing the closest point on axis to ray."
    },
    {
      "id": "bool-7b0171",
      "name": "bool",
      "category": "AxisPositionGizmo",
      "signature": "bool(Target, World Ray, Custom Destination Func)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "UAxisPositionGizmo*"
        },
        {
          "name": "World Ray",
          "type": "FCustomDestinationParams&"
        },
        {
          "name": "Custom Destination Func",
          "type": "FVector& OutputPoint )>",
          "default": "[](const FCustomDestinationParams& Params, FVector& OutputPoint"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "TUniqueFunction<",
      "docs": "If ShouldUseCustomDestinationFunc() returns true, this function gets queried to get a destination point.\nThe gizmo parameter will then be picked in such a way that the dragged location moves to the closest point\non the axis to the destination point (optionally offset by the start click position relative the axis origin,\nif bCustomDestinationAlignsAxisOrigin is true, to align the axis origin itself). Can be used, for example,\nto align to items in the scene."
    },
